.TH STAMP 1ptk "November 2026" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stamp \- apply configurable timestamps to patterns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/local/bin/stamp
[
.I -dhjtv
] [
.BI -m " c"
] [
.BI -n " #"
]
.I pattern ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stamp
processes the provided
.I pattern
arguments and applies timestamps based on the specified options. 
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-j
Use the Julian date format.
.TP
.B \-m \fIc\fR
Use character 
.I c
to mark the location of the timestamp.
.TP
.B \-n \fI#\fR
Use a numeric stamp instead of the default date.
.TP
.B \-t
Use the time in the stamp.
.TP
.B \-v
Increase verbosity.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
.B stamp -t "%s"
.EE
Apply a timestamp including the time to the string template.
.SH AUTHORS
Paul Kinney.
